window.docContents[191].resolve({"/Smallstep/#Type-Systems--Smallstep___-Small-step-Operational-Semantics--Multi-Step-Reduction":{"contents":"\n\ninductive Multi {X : Type} (R : Relation X) : X → X → Prop where\n  | refl (x : X) : Multi R x x\n  | step (x y z : X) (h1 : R x y) (h2 : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z\ninductive Multi {X : Type} (R : Relation X) : X → X → Prop where\n  | refl (x : X) : Multi R x x\n  | step (x y z : X) (h1 : R x y) (h2 : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z\ninductive Multi {X : Type} (R : Relation X) : X → X → Prop where\n  | refl (x : X) : Multi R x x\n  | step (x y z : X) (h1 : R x y) (h2 : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z\n\n\nI would make some arguments implicit to proivde a cleaner interface (FYI the mathlib version)\n\n\n\nWe write ⟶* for the Multi Step relation on terms\n\nnotation:40 t:41 \" ⟶* \" t':41 => Multi Step t t'\nnotation:40 t:41 \" ⟶* \" t':41 => Multi Step t t'\nnotation:40 t:41 \" ⟶* \" t':41 => Multi Step t t'\n\n\nThe relation Multi R has several crucial properties.\n\n\n\nattribute [refl] Multi.refl\n\nexample : (.c 5 : Tm) ⟶* .c 5 := by rfl\nattribute [refl] Multi.refl\n\nexample : (.c 5 : Tm) ⟶* .c 5 := by rfl\nattribute [refl] Multi.refl\n\nexample : (.c 5 : Tm) ⟶* .c 5 := by rfl\n\n\n\n\nexample : (.p (.c 1) (.c 2)) ⟶* .c (1 + 2) := by\n  apply Multi.step (y := .c (1 + 2))\n  · exact .plus 1 2\n  · rfl\nexample : (.p (.c 1) (.c 2)) ⟶* .c (1 + 2) := by\n  apply Multi.step (y := .c (1 + 2))\n  · exact .plus 1 2\n  · rfl\nexample : (.p (.c 1) (.c 2)) ⟶* .c (1 + 2) := by\n  apply Multi.step (y := .c (1 + 2))\n  · exact .plus 1 2\n  · rfl\n\n\n\n\ntheorem multi_single {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y : X) (h : R x y) :\n    Multi R x y :=\n  .step x y y h (.refl y)\ntheorem multi_single {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y : X) (h : R x y) :\n    Multi R x y :=\n  .step x y y h (.refl y)\ntheorem multi_single {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y : X) (h : R x y) :\n    Multi R x y :=\n  .step x y y h (.refl y)\n\n\n\n\ntheorem multi_trans {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y z : X)\n    (g : Multi R x y) (h : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z := by\n  induction g with\n  | refl a => exact h\n  | step a b c h1 h2 ih => exact .step a b z h1 (ih h)\ntheorem multi_trans {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y z : X)\n    (g : Multi R x y) (h : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z := by\n  induction g with\n  | refl a => exact h\n  | step a b c h1 h2 ih => exact .step a b z h1 (ih h)\ntheorem multi_trans {X : Type} (R : Relation X) (x y z : X)\n    (g : Multi R x y) (h : Multi R y z) : Multi R x z := by\n  induction g with\n  | refl a => exact h\n  | step a b c h1 h2 ih => exact .step a b z h1 (ih h)\n\n\n\n\nWhich of the following relations on numbers cannot be expressed as\nMulti R for some R?(A) less than or equal\n(B) strictly less than\n(C) equal\n(D) none of the above\n\n(B) strictly less than\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009Smallstep: Small-step Operational Semantics","header":"3.4. Multi-Step Reduction","id":"/Smallstep/#Type-Systems--Smallstep___-Small-step-Operational-Semantics--Multi-Step-Reduction"}});